                                                    <div id="Button4" class="tabcontent links">
                                                        <p class="factitle">Teaching Innovation</p>
                                                        <p class="facpara">
                                                            Innovative teaching practices in a class call for a
                                                            deliberate move away from passive teaching approaches to a
                                                            more active, learner-centered methodology that incorporates
                                                            assessment, application, and continuous feedback. One of the
                                                            primary techniques used by me is the consistent inclusion of
                                                            quizzes, assignments, case studies, fieldwork, and
                                                            presentations for all important concepts taught. The purpose
                                                            of using these techniques is not just to assess the
                                                            students' performance but also to consolidate their learning
                                                            process through repetition and reflection. Immediate
                                                            feedback is provided to the students right after every
                                                            activity. This immediate feedback system helps students
                                                            recognize weaknesses and areas of improvement, thus
                                                            improving their understanding of the subject matter. This
                                                            continuous cycle of learning and feedback results in a high
                                                            level of conceptual clarity and discipline among the
                                                            students.<br>
                                                            Apart from using the traditional method of assessment, one
                                                            of the innovative teaching approaches used by me in finance
                                                            and management classes is practical-based learning. Students
                                                            are made to solve practical-based problems related to
                                                            finance, which include preparing financial statements, ratio
                                                            analysis, budgeting, and financial modeling. One unique
                                                            thing about this strategy is that MS Excel is used as a
                                                            problem-solving and analytic instrument in class. When doing
                                                            problems related to MS Excel, students get to practice
                                                            organizing information, manipulating formulas, performing
                                                            financial calculations, and modeling.<br>
                                                            MS Excel does not only involve simple computations. It
                                                            teaches students to optimize problems and manage resources
                                                            effectively. This includes using Excel features such as
                                                            Solver, Goal Seek, and scenario analysis. By learning how
                                                            businesses solve complex issues through MS Excel, students
                                                            can gain a better understanding of approaches for solving
                                                            cost-minimizing and profit-maximizing problems in the real
                                                            world. The students will thus be able to develop important
                                                            competencies in analyzing problems quantitatively and
                                                            logically.<br>
                                                            These exercises and assignments help the students build
                                                            important skills related to analyzing data and making
                                                            decisions in a logical way. In addition, students will feel
                                                            confident dealing with voluminous amounts of data and
                                                            reporting on them professionally. More importantly, students
                                                            will gain experience in business scenarios that involve
                                                            complex managerial decisions. This kind of experience will
                                                            greatly prepare the students for working in areas like
                                                            finance, marketing, consulting, and operations management.
                                                            A further critical aspect of my innovation as a teacher is
                                                            the use of interactive learning. Sessions in the classroom
                                                            will be interactive by having students discuss cases, engage
                                                            in groups, and solve problems related to the topic at hand.
                                                            Sometimes, learners will be assigned groups where they will
                                                            analyze real business situations, offer various solutions to
                                                            the problem, and come up with solutions. This strategy not
                                                            only increases the understanding of the concept learned but
                                                            also improves interpersonal skills. Mini-projects and field
                                                            work will add to this learning experience.<br>
                                                            Presentations of assignments and case analyses in class are
                                                            also another approach to improving the quality of learning
                                                            in my class. Through presentations, students can improve
                                                            their communication and public speaking skills as they get a
                                                            chance to defend their analyses in front of other learners.
                                                            Learners can learn from one another during this learning
                                                            process since each will bring some different approaches and
                                                            perspectives to the discussion.<br>
                                                            The use of constant assessments, practical applications of
                                                            theories, and computer-based tools such as Microsoft Excel
                                                            greatly contributes to the quality of education being
                                                            offered. It not only enhances memory but also ensures
                                                            greater understanding. In doing so, these methods will not
                                                            only provide academic proficiency among the students but
                                                            will make them professional and ready for the corporate
                                                            world.<br>
                                                            To conclude, my innovative ideas about teaching revolve
                                                            around closing the distance between theory and practice
                                                            through various activities and constant feedback. Such an
                                                            approach helps in developing a proper mindset and skills in
                                                            the students which will assist them in future life and
                                                            career.

                                                        </p>

                                                    </div>

